{#- The first visit's one question (2026-09-10, targum-internal#243): a browser that
    says it speaks a language the conversation can gloss in — Russian, today — is
    asked once, in that language, whether the lines under the Hebrew should be in it.
    Never guessed silently: the stored answer changes only on the press. Drawn by
    `first.js`, only where it applies; hidden otherwise, and gone once answered. -#}
<p class="chat-first-lang" id="chat-first-lang" hidden>
  <span id="chat-first-ask"></span>
  <button type="button" class="chat-first-yes" id="chat-first-yes"></button>
  <button type="button" class="chat-first-no" id="chat-first-no"></button>
</p>
